# Wave C.a — Lazy marketing catalog bindings

## Problem

`packages/guest-workspace-runtime` collapsed portal/marketing **direct** product deps, but `workspace-marketing-catalog-bindings.generated.ts` still **statically** imported:

```ts
import { denaliMarketingCatalogSurface } from "@app-tour/workspace-denali/host/marketing/…";
```

Any import of `@app-tour/guest-workspace-runtime/marketing-catalog` therefore pulls Denali into the marketing cold graph. Theme loaders were already dynamic; catalog was not. Portal/marketing `transpilePackages` lists remain a separate install/transpile concern (Wave C.b).

## Decision

Codegen (`generateMarketingCatalogBindings`) emits:

| Export | Shape |
| ------ | ----- |
| `hasMarketingCatalogSurface(pluginId)` | **Sync** — `Set` of manifest ids with `marketingCatalog` (no product import) |
| `resolveMarketingCatalogSurface(pluginId)` | **Async** — `await import(specifier)` per id, string-literal only |

Marketing app helpers/components that need the surface `await` the resolver (most catalog UI is already async RSC).

Cold-path guard includes the generated bindings file (`staticProductImports === 0`).

## Out of scope (Wave C.b+)

- ~~Codegen of `transpilePackages` arrays (drop-in DX only)~~ → **DONE** in [`wave-c-guest-transpile-packages.mdoc`](./wave-c-guest-transpile-packages.mdoc)
- Removing product packages from `guest-workspace-runtime/package.json` (pnpm still needs them for dynamic import resolution; shrink requires optional/peer split or per-tenant builds) — **Wave C.c**

## Verify

```bash
pnpm run generate:workspace-registry
pnpm run guard:p4-cold-path-fan-in
pnpm --filter @apps/marketing exec node --import tsx --test \
  test/marketing-workspace-denali-boundary.spec.ts \
  test/derive-catalog-filter-options.spec.ts \
  test/filter-marketing-catalog-items.spec.ts \
  test/build-catalog-list-card-summary.spec.ts \
  test/resolve-marketing-catalog-category-label.spec.ts
```
